  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "When Walter drove up to the gasoline pump, he noticed that his gasoline tank was \\(\\dfrac18\\) full. He purchased \\(7.5\\) gallons of gasoline for \\(\\$10.\\) With this additional gasoline, his gasoline tank was then \\(\\dfrac58\\) full. The number of gallons of gasoline his tank holds when it is full is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8.75\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(11.5\\)",
    "D": "\\(15\\)",
    "E": "\\(22.5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The purchased gasoline accounts for the increase in the fraction of the tank that is full:\n\\[\n\\frac58-\\frac18=\\frac48=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThus \\(7.5\\) gallons fill half the tank. The full tank holds twice that amount:\n\\[\n7.5\\div\\frac12=7.5\\cdot2=15.\n\\]\nThe capacity is \\(15\\) gallons, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
